    "title": "Actors Amy Madigan and Ed Harris Have Been Married for Over Four Decades",
    "text": "2 min readAt the Oscars this evening, Best Supporting Actress nominee Amy Madigan will be supported by her husband of over four decades, fellow actor Ed Harris.“He loved it,” Madigan said of Harris’s reaction to watching her in Weapons, the film for which she’s nominated. “He’s known me a long time and he saw all the parts of myself melded into Aunt Gladys. So, I have a very supportive family, my daughter also, so I’m very lucky.”Monica Schipper//Getty ImagesAmy Madigan and Ed Harris at the 83rd Annual Golden Globe Awards.Madigan, 75, and Harris, also 75, have been married since 1983. They have one daughter, Lily, who followed her parents into acting. “We just love each other and we work really hard at that and in our work,” Madigan said about their relationship at the New York Film Critics Circle Awards in January.Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowHere, what to know about Madigan’s husband Ed Harris, a four-time Oscar nominee:He’s from New Jersey.Bob Riha Jr//Getty ImagesHarris in 1997.Harris, born in 1950, grew up in New Jersey and went on to study at Columbia University, where he was on the football team. After his family moved to New Mexico, he transferred to the University of Oklahoma, and then to the California Institute of Arts, where he graduated with a Bachelor of Fine Arts in 1975.He made his acting debut in the 70s.Harris has had a long and fruitful career in movies and television, and was nominated for Oscars for his performances in Apollo 13 (1995), The Truman Show (1998), Pollock (2000), and The Hours (2002). As the Man in Black in Westworld, which aired from 2018 to 2022, he earned an Emmy nomination. He most recently appeared in How to Make a Killing and will next feature in The Dink, a sports comedy film premiering this summer.Harris and Madigan married in 1983.Pool DENIZE/PELLETIER//Getty ImagesThe couple in 1985.The couple began dating in 1981, after she saw him in the 1980 play Cowboy. “It was like something you see in a movie or hear in a song. I just thought, ‘Well, there he is.’ It was obvious to me that I'd see him again,” she told Life in 1985.They co-starred in the 1984 film Places in the Heart, and married in 1983 while in production for the movie. “The acting thing is so intimate and personal,” Harris told the Chicago Tribune in 1985 of working with Madigan. “If we’re not working together... you can’t really talk about your day very well. When you’re working together, though, there’s so much that is shared, so much unspoken thought and emotion that goes into the work, that it really draws you closer.”Emily Burack (she/her) is the Deputy Digital Editor for Town & Country, where she covers entertainment, celebrities, the royals, and a wide range of other topics. Before joining T&C, she was the deputy managing editor at Hey Alma, a Jewish culture site. Follow her @emburack on Instagram, Twitter, and other social media platforms.",
